<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abha is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asir">Asir</a> region in south-western Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, standing about 2,200 metres up in the Sarawat mountains. In the 19th century it was the seat of the Al Aidh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> of Asir until an Ottoman army took it in 1871–1872, and it was incorporated into the Saudi state in the early 1920s. Its mild climate has made it a summer resort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abha.jpg" alt="Abha" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: أشخاص متنوعين ولكن هناك صورة مصورة من أمانة منطقة عسير وصورة مصورة من عوض زارب · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abha_city.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
